  "term": "trigeminal nerve",
  "definition": "The trigeminal nerve is the fifth and largest cranial nerve. It has a large sensory division that carries input from the face, mouth, teeth, and related muscles and joints through its ophthalmic, maxillary, and mandibular branches, and a smaller motor division that supplies the muscles used for chewing.",
